{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266497-on-fighting-slavery-with-words-plot-help","id":1266497,"title":"On Fighting Slavery with Words - Plot Help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-11-11T14:38:04-08:00","id":1266497,"title":"On Fighting Slavery with Words - Plot Help","content":"So, I'm running a game of Exalted, and my players (a pair of Twilights, one craft-focused and one a sorcerer, and a political Eclipse) are in a trading city in the Scavenger Lands, and the Eclipse has taken it upon herself to try and get the de facto ruler of the city, a godblood head of the local bigshot noble house, to restrict or preferably stop Guild trade of slaves through the city. And I have no idea how to deal with this.<br /> <br /> Now, it's not as unrealistic as it could be, seeing as the nation they're currently in doesn't use slaves (they just trade in them, toooootally different thing), but there's still a lot of money to be made via taxation, buying low and selling high and so on. Does anyone have any advice on how to handle this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T14:57:20-08:00","id":1266499,"title":"","content":"What does the Prince feel about<b></b>:<br /> Slavery<br /> Guild influence<br /> Foreign merchants<br /> <br /> And what do the common people think? Do they love or hate the Guild? <br /> <br /> What are relations like with the countries that a)buy slaves, and b)provide slaves?<br /> <br /> Who is making the money? How does the Prince tax the slave merchants?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T15:28:29-08:00","id":1266504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266497-on-fighting-slavery-with-words-plot-help#post1266497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm running a game of Exalted, and my players (a pair of Twilights, one craft-focused and one a sorcerer, and a political Eclipse) are in a trading city in the Scavenger Lands, and the Eclipse has taken it upon herself to try and get the de facto ruler of the city, a godblood head of the local bigshot noble house, to restrict or preferably stop Guild trade of slaves through the city. And I have no idea how to deal with this.<br /> <br /> Now, it's not as unrealistic as it could be, seeing as the nation they're currently in doesn't use slaves (they just trade in them, toooootally different thing), but there's still a lot of money to be made via taxation, buying low and selling high and so on. Does anyone have any advice on how to handle this?</div> </div> </div> </div>You would have to find the political will to make it happen. Asking someone who clearly has no moral qualms about the issue to cut off a big chunk of their tax revenue requires you to provide some sort of incentive. Are there lucrative trade opportunities to be had by being seen as someone who would stand up to the Guild, or would cutting out one piece of the Guild's pie cause the Guild to start messing with their economy in other ways?<br /> <br /> Don't underestimate the economic pressure the Guild can bring down on a city, especially in their backyard such as it were. Your players would need to find a way to make the idea enticing while minimizing the chance of it sending the city into a recession.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T15:29:04-08:00","id":1266505,"title":"","content":"You are three solars, you can produce more Capital then the whole city sees from all their various industries and trade. You could offer a variety of options such as:<br /> <br /> Creating a magically prosperous Orchard with Sorcerous working that creates natural deserts.<br /> <br /> Agreeing to summon Demons and Or Elementals to provide free labor for civic projects and industries like Mining.<br /> <br /> Provide the city with wonders and artifacts such as a system of free hot and cold clean plumbing. A magical orchestra that plays every sunset and sunrise. A grove of brass bamboo that is easy to harvest as natural growing piping. A housing infrastructure for the ancestor spirits of the city. A giant fish that can be harvested for fillets but regenerates every night. A system of schools libraries and Hospitals with spirits dedicated to teaching new generations.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sky\u2019s the limit. It depends how much you want to spend time on appeasing the city. Would they prefer the taxes from slaves or would they like free indoor plumbing? Or a donated Armory of professionally crafted weapons and Armor and a giant bronze guardian that never sleeps and always guards the gates. Or just building a couple layers to the city state professionally created underground?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T20:59:05-08:00","id":1266602,"title":"","content":"I'd say good general advice for <i>any</i> political plot, not just this one, is to identify three things:<br /> 1) Who is going to make the ultimate decision, and what are their motivations? That is, who do you have to convince, and how will you do it? In this case, it sounds like it's the head of this noble house. <br /> 2) Who will oppose the decision, what are their motivations, and what will they do to prevent it? In this case, the Guild is an obvious choice, and the Guild is generally known to be pretty ruthless. But don't think just in terms of assassination squads being sent to take out the PCs - the Guild has the ability to exert substantial economic pressure as well, so the Eclipse needs to be prepared for the local Guild factor telling the ruler &quot;sure, we can cut off slave trading. Of course, that means our caravans won't be profitable enough to run through here, so we'll also be cutting off all <i>other</i> trading too. Good luck finding another source for all those luxury goods we bring!&quot;<br /> 3) Similar to 2, but who <i>supports </i>the decision, their motivation, etc. Obviously, in this case, abolitionists are likely allies, but this can be the place to present some more uncomfortable alliances as well. For example, maybe a Guild factor is secretly working to eliminate the slave trade - because she controls the trade along another route, and ending it here makes her own profits swell. <br /> <br /> Once you've determined what the people involved want, and what they'll do to get what they want, I find plot tends to develop quite naturally. The PCs will try to convince the people they need to, and will have to make deals with allies and the ruler to get the support they need, while meanwhile, their opponents will be trying to counteract them, and thus require the PCs to take action against them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T23:27:06-08:00","id":1266618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266497-on-fighting-slavery-with-words-plot-help#post1266497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now, it's not as unrealistic as it could be, seeing as the nation they're currently in doesn't use slaves (they just trade in them, toooootally different thing), but there's still a lot of money to be made via taxation, buying low and selling high and so on. Does anyone have any advice on how to handle this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you looking for advice on narrative progression from the characters' actions and successes, or how to engage with the premise with the system?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T04:13:43-08:00","id":1266663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266497-on-fighting-slavery-with-words-plot-help?p=1266618#post1266618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you looking for advice on narrative progression from the characters' actions and successes, or how to engage with the premise with the system?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly the former, though advice on the latter would be very welcome as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 11-12-2018, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T04:21:43-08:00","id":1266664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266497-on-fighting-slavery-with-words-plot-help?p=1266663#post1266663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly the former, bout advice on the latter would be very welcome as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You could, probably/maybe, use the Projects/Leadership-system, from the core book, as a start. And let that guide you with what scenes to play up (aquiring the necessary assets, how they go about it etc.), how long it would take, and what consequences they might encounter on the way (or as side effects after the fact).<br /> <br /> Edit: Though I haven't had a chance to try it myself yet, so I don't know how well it works, personally, yet","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1920-kim","name":"Kim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T04:34:18-08:00","id":1266666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266497-on-fighting-slavery-with-words-plot-help?p=1266664#post1266664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You could, probably/maybe, use the Projects/Leadership-system, from the core book, as a start. And let that guide you with what scenes to play up (aquiring the necessary assets, how they go about it etc.), how long it would take, and what consequences they might encounter on the way (or as side effects after the fact).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, I feel like in a scenario such as this, with the described characterisation of the Eclipse and the fact that they're not really in a position of authority but are more of a foreign interloper, it would be better, it would be more fitting to use the social system to represent somebody making impassioned arguments to sway people's hearts and minds. Like, sure, there are going to be contrary Intimacies to contend with, but that lends the scenario some breadth and texture, a nice sequence of instilling and degrading complementary Intimacies and finding the right arguments to make the effective appeals.<br /> <br /> I'm often all for injecting a measure of realism, but something about the initial description sparks my sense that this is one of those cases where it's better to lean on the romantic, mythic, epic angle of a highly charismatic and impassioned person calling people to the common good with their speech.<br /> <br /> So, consequences. If the society doesn't actually utilise the slave labour themselves, that takes away the question of how you're going to integrate a lot of suddenly emancipated slaves. Answering the question of how the change in revenue plays out largely depends on what that money was being earmarked for; if it's something important and necessary like paying for mercenaries or public utilities,, the circle might feel a responsibility to stick around and help shore some of those things up. The Eclipse might want to go over the public books and help with a bit of refinancing, such as devising alternative tax schemes that can make up for the shortfall without being too burdensome on any one sector; same thing might go in a different direction if the cash was necessary for paying off a public debt (that one might require a bit of chicanery, in which one basically designs a kind of documentation shell game such that the buck for who actually owes the creditors keeps getting shifted around so nobody ever actually pays anything). If it's about certain maintenance, those Twilights might be put to good use in fixing some things up and making them divinely enduring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T05:02:09-08:00","id":1266669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266497-on-fighting-slavery-with-words-plot-help?p=1266505#post1266505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sky\u2019s the limit. It depends how much you want to spend time on appeasing the city. Would they prefer the taxes from slaves or would they like free indoor plumbing? Or a donated Armory of professionally crafted weapons and Armor and a giant bronze guardian that never sleeps and always guards the gates. Or just building a couple layers to the city state professionally created underground?</div> </div> </div> </div>How open the trio can be about being Solar might impose a limit. Some people might prefer taxes from slaves over indoor plumbing from anathema.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T08:38:17-08:00","id":1266707,"title":"","content":"A strategy a character of mine recently employed was to appropriate a symbol of a pre-existing aboltionist movement (dying her hair blue) and used it to show her patronage of a former slave in a fighting tournament knowing full well that people would emulate her. Thus making the movement seem way stronger in the city than it actually is and a factor she can use to discourage ventures that involve slavery in a &quot;I can't promise you won't get lynched&quot; sort of way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T21:26:28-08:00","id":1266859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266497-on-fighting-slavery-with-words-plot-help?p=1266663#post1266663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly the former, though advice on the latter would be very welcome as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Latter\u2019s easy:<br /> <br /> 1. Write Intimacy list and social stats for the noble.<br /> <br /> 2. Sit back and watch the show.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T21:33:22-08:00","id":1266860,"title":"","content":"Don't forget 3.) Make sure failure is interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T22:14:46-08:00","id":1266867,"title":"","content":"Consider that the Guild is going to look unfavorably upon their business being interrupted, and will probably exert pressure to conform to their preferred status quo in unexpected ways--both underhanded and even overtly violent. This shouldn't undermine the PC's actions, but should clarify the sheer scope of the problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T22:40:25-08:00","id":1266871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266497-on-fighting-slavery-with-words-plot-help?p=1266860#post1266860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget 3.) Make sure failure is interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is definitely good advice, but I'd add another: make sure <i>success</i> is interesting too. In my experience with Exalted, a character, particularly a Solar, will probably succeed at the goals they set themselves, at least those within their speciality. So, make sure that when they do succeed, there are consequences for that. Note, I <i>don't</i> mean a GM screwjob, where the characters get their desire, and it turns out to be totally horrible. But all actions have consequences, and some of those consequences will be things the characters didn't intend and don't necessarily want. In this case, I would say to think about who controls the slave trade in the city, and figure out what will happen if they can't ship through the region any more, and both the sellers and the buyers of the slaves. All of those people could have negative reactions to the slave trade being cut off in the city - the Guild, as I already mentioned, could cut off more than just the slave trade, denying rich people luxuries and poor people necessities, depending on the local economy. If the slave-sellers are faced with smaller demand for slaves, they might start selling them to other places, which could well be worse than previous - if they started selling directly to Fair Folk, for instance. And the slave-buyers, dealing with a sudden shortage of slaves, might start raiding their neighbours for new &quot;stock&quot;, which might include the territory of the city-state the characters are in.<br /> <br /> Now, I'll throw one big caveat in here - I think abolitionist ideals are absolutely a good thing to encourage, so my own approach to these sorts of consequences for success would emphasize the idea that stopping the slave trade in the city-state definitely did some good. Make sure to mention that even if the trade is taking a new route, it's a harder or longer one, meaning fewer slaves are being transported over it, and thus fewer are being enslaved in the first place. This is just realistic, I feel - if there really was no difference between the current route and some other one, then why is this a difficult decision for the traders? They'd just move to a new route the moment anyone even raised the prospect of forbidding the trade along the current route. So the fact that there even is a significant conflict suggests that other routes are less good. Anyway, the point I'm making is, when it comes to ending slavery, it's <i>even more</i> important to make sure that while you present success as having consequences, that you don't diminish the success in the process.<br /> <br /> I guess what I'm trying to say overall is that each success should broaden the scope of the characters' actions, at least slightly. If they successfully end the slave trade in the city-state, make sure they know about how the change is affecting the trade in surrounding regions, and point out that if they want to end slavery entirely, they're going to have to expand outward and deal with the larger circumstances. If you do this consistently, you can create a natural progression where the characters end up trying to conquer the world, or at least a significant fraction of it, just to keep achieving greater and greater stages of their goals. And that's a plot that should keep you busy for a long time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T06:46:30-08:00","id":1266938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266497-on-fighting-slavery-with-words-plot-help?p=1266871#post1266871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now, I'll throw one big caveat in here - I think abolitionist ideals are absolutely a good thing to encourage, so my own approach to these sorts of consequences for success would emphasize the idea that stopping the slave trade in the city-state definitely did some good. Make sure to mention that even if the trade is taking a new route, it's a harder or longer one, meaning fewer slaves are being transported over it, and thus fewer are being enslaved in the first place. This is just realistic, I feel - if there really was no difference between the current route and some other one, then why is this a difficult decision for the traders? They'd just move to a new route the moment anyone even raised the prospect of forbidding the trade along the current route. So the fact that there even is a significant conflict suggests that other routes are less good. Anyway, the point I'm making is, when it comes to ending slavery, it's <i>even more</i> important to make sure that while you present success as having consequences, that you don't diminish the success in the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wholeheartedly disagree. In all things, the Solars should be impactful, regardless of whether their goals align with.. anything. If they manage to convince a noble to begin slave trading, you should present their success as having consequences, but still don't diminish the impact of their achievement. Hell, if they convince a noble to make Tyrant Lizards an endangered species, you should... well, I've said it enough now - present the successes with consequences, but don't diminish their achievement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T07:54:20-08:00","id":1266948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266497-on-fighting-slavery-with-words-plot-help?p=1266938#post1266938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wholeheartedly disagree. In all things, the Solars should be impactful, regardless of whether their goals align with.. anything. If they manage to convince a noble to begin slave trading, you should present their success as having consequences, but still don't diminish the impact of their achievement.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I was unclear, apologies! That is actually exactly what I was saying - success should be successful, and achieve more or less the goal the character set out to achieve. And I was trying to say that, in the case of a goal like ending slavery, that I'd want to particularly emphasize that it <i>was</i> successful, and that any consequences shouldn't be &quot;you've just made things worse everywhere&quot;. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T07:55:12-08:00","id":1266949,"title":"","content":"How are you disagreeing? You said you think &quot;you should present their success as having consequences, but still don't diminish the impact of their achievement&quot;.<br /> <br /> Kelly said to &quot;<i>make sure that while you present success as having consequences, that you don't diminish the success in the process&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Isn't that the same?<br /> <br /> Edit: Ninja'd<br /> <br /> So a couple of things about abolitionism.<br /> <br /> Britain freed all slaves in Britain in the 1770s, banned the slave trade in 1808, and eventually freed all slaves by the 1830s. Now, previously, it hadn't been the case that everyone thought the slave trade was awesome (except the elites who owned the slaves, of course). But what they thought was that:<br /> Slavery is bad, but, you know, it's not like really, really bad.<br /> Slavery is just the way of the world. There's not any alternative.<br /> Slavery is bad... but I mean, the economy would collapse without it.<br /> Slavery is bad... but the slaves are all savages anyway, so not much has changed, it might even be good for them.<br /> Slavery is bad... but what can I do?<br /> <br /> The abolitionists used various tactics to get slavery banned, but essentially what they did was to convince the British people that slavery was something they could actually change, and they should. They appealed to people's moral sensibilities by getting freed slaves to give talks about the conditions, they hinted to the military and merchants that this would be a great way to screw over rivals like the Dutch (by boarding slave ships and freeing the slaves), they argued that the economic costs weren't that high (when slavery was eventually banned across the Empire, it was reckoned at 5% of Britain's GDP for a single year, which isn't that much) and by getting people involved in lobbying parliament they showed people that actually there was something they could do about it. They also played to British people's sense of superiority by encouraging them to think about how morally superior this would show Britain to be compared to other Empires. And finally, of course, they explained how most average men on the street, who didn't own slaves, would not be seriously impacted.<br /> Of course, they didn't convince everyone. But they didn't need to, just enough people to get it banned.<br /> <br /> <br /> There are two points here; first, they made multiple arguments to different people about different things. For some they appealed to their arrogance, others (the Navy) their greed, others their morals, others their religion. They played down the costs and played up the benefits. There was an economic cost in the end, but they managed to convince people to accept it.<br /> <br /> The other point is that they didn't do this by appealing just to the King, or even just to the politicians. It was a mass campaign, in an age when only rich men could vote (in an <i>extremely</i> corrupt system). Why bother convincing people who don't actually make the decision? Because even monarchs think about how their people would react.<br /> <br /> <br /> I was reading about British responses to the American Civil War. The Confederacy hoped to ally with Britain against the Union. And many British elites wanted to join the Confederacy (the Prime Minister's family had originally gained their wealth from Caribbean slave plantations). But the common people generally supported the Union, even though the Civil War was causing unemployment in Britain, and so the government didn't believe they could get support to ally with the Confederacy.<br /> <br /> <br /> Your PCs are going to want to convince the Prince of course. But even if they convince the Prince it's bad, is he going to want to piss off powerful mercantile interests who might overthrow him? On the other hand, if you can get the people clamouring for the abolition of the slave trade, even if he doesn't care, he may ban it.<br /> <br /> And of course, the final point is that people are sometimes willing to take an economic hit for morality. It's hard to convince them to do so, but it's not impossible. Not everyone is 100% cynical and amoral.<br /> <br /> Edit: I'm sure others can talk about the success of abolitionism in other places, but I don't know so much of the details about those.<br /> <br /> One other example I'll mention which happened in various places is that... they just got invaded, and forced to stop involvement in the slave trade. The Normans invaded Britain and (not instantly, but gradually) stopped the slave trade. In the 19th century, the British sometimes attacked places involved in the slave trade, which made it less appealing. China often justifies its annexation of Tibet (sorry, eternal rule which has always existed) by pointing out they banned slavery. There's some evidence that slavery had already ceased to exist by the 1940s, and there's an argument about whether hereditary household servants were slaves or not, but anyway. <br /> <br /> My point is, at the end of the day, your PCs could always just seize control of the city and ban it. Or murder all the slavers (that's how our Lunar stopped the Slave Trade in Azure. Once she'd murdered and eaten 30 slave traders, the slave trade dried to a trickle).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-13-2018, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T08:35:26-08:00","id":1266964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266497-on-fighting-slavery-with-words-plot-help?p=1266948#post1266948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess I was unclear, apologies! That is actually exactly what I was saying - success should be successful, and achieve more or less the goal the character set out to achieve. And I was trying to say that, in the case of a goal like ending slavery, that I'd want to particularly emphasize that it <i>was</i> successful, and that any consequences shouldn't be &quot;you've just made things worse everywhere&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, no, it appears that I was unclear. I meant that it feels wrong to make a success or failure more or less consequential simply by virtue of anyone's personal agreement with the aim, which, to me, is what you're saying you would want to do. If a nation relies on slavery and you abolish it without placing something else in its stead, then you get to walk away with a happy feeling, but you've just screwed that nation right up and the consequences of your wanton dogoodery should resound no more and no less clearly, regardless of how you personally feel about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T09:35:25-08:00","id":1266983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266497-on-fighting-slavery-with-words-plot-help?p=1266964#post1266964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant that it feels wrong to make a success or failure more or less consequential simply by virtue of anyone's personal agreement with the aim, which, to me, is what you're saying you would want to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that was what you were saying, then, well, I disagree. Exalted's a roleplaying game, which means that considering the real participants' feelings and reactions is more important to me than an abstract consideration of &quot;what is absolutely the most realistic thing to happen&quot;. Slavery's a fraught subject, and deserves more careful handling than some others. Also, &quot;most realistic&quot; is, in my experience, something of an illusion in any case. &quot;Realism&quot; is quite often used to justify simply continuing our real-world prejudices in fiction (see umpteen-million arguments about how women can't be warriors, for instance, despite there being ample evidence that there <i>were</i> female warriors in the real world in basically all time periods). So I would avoid worrying too much about &quot;realistic&quot; consequences, and just remember that history contains plenty of times where things really did work out for the better, overall.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T10:59:34-08:00","id":1267009,"title":"","content":"I myself like to have believable realism. Verisimilitude.<br /> <br /> But... abolishing slavery is better. I mean, not for slave owners, but for the entire population as a whole. That's just fact. There may well be problematic side-effects, and these might be long-term, but then, there's problematic side-effects of having slaves (and I do mean side-effects, on top of the obvious problem of the slaves having miserable lives).<br /> <br /> Inequality will decrease, which leads to more stable societies, lower crime, etc. As slave raiding reduces, the no-longer-targeted countries will develop better economies. With less work as slave raiders, in the short term mercenaries may turn to banditry and destabilise stuff, but in the long term, there will be less soldiers, which means more people can turn to productive pursuits. Similarly, slave overseers and jailers will no longer be necessary, and can do more productive things. Related to that, violence and oppression will be required less, which will create a less violent culture and reduce crime generally. There will be a reduction in the slave-holding class, weakening the power of elites. Many countries (though not all) have justified slavery via socially divisive ideologies, and without that need, these will decrease, creating better social harmony. And a big benefit of course, is that slaves are more likely to improve their skills and situation, further developing the region.<br /> <br /> And then of course, there's slave revolts, which obviously kill people, damage property, etc, and stopping slavery means stopping slave revolts. Not having to worry about slave revolts will allow the army to more effectively defend against outside threats instead, as they can be stationed more at borders than near slave plantations.<br /> <br /> Altogether, when the PCs stop the slave trade in this city, especially if they then go to other countries and do the same, the overall economy of the region will increase, it will become more peaceful, and more stable.<br /> (Though obviously you'll have to find something else to do with prisoners instead of selling them. But there's plenty of alternatives. And allowing the sale of prisoners as slaves may be a way to exile/punish dangerous people, but they're still dangerous somewhere else, and the option of slavery creates perverse incentives to arrest people on trumped-up charges. West African economies were devastated partly because some Kings kept finding excuses to arrest people so they could sell them for profit, which of course in the long run actually meant less subjects. But rulers often suffer from short-termism.)<br /> <br /> Admittedly, some of these may take a while. And it may not be realistic to show an immediate beneficial effect in the place where the slave trade is banned (obviously the place they're getting slaves is going to have a pretty quick beneficial effect) because the benefits are general to the region, rather than specific to that city (which doesn't have slaves itself anyway). But ultimately, banning the slave trade is beneficial for society, and so it's not unrealistic for Kelly to show players that it is beneficial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-13-2018, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T11:26:53-08:00","id":1267025,"title":"","content":"Something else to consider for Exalted in terms of banning slavery.<br /> Looking at history again, and to quote a priest involved in the Abolition Society: <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John Newton</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not qualified... to consider the African slave trade merely in a political light... The best human policy is that which is connected with a reverential regard to Almighty God, the supreme governor of the earth. Every plan, which aims at the welfare of a nation, in defiance of his authority and laws, however apparently wise, will prove to be essentially defective, and, if persisted in, ruinous. The righteous Lord loveth righteousness, and he has engaged to plead the cause and vindicate the wrongs of the oppressed. It is righteousness that exalteth a nation ; and wickedness is the present reproach, and will, sooner or later, unless repentance intervene, prove the ruin of any people.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <br /> Essentially, Gods are a powerful force, and may bless or curse people<br /> <br /> If the PCs can find some spirits who hate the slave trade for various reasons (it could be because they're God of Freedom or something, but it could also be random stuff, like, for example, slaves don't live in proper houses, so the God of Houses doesn't like the slave trade, or their use keeps costs in big plantations lower than those of smallholding farms, so the God of Freeholding Farms doesn't like them), they could convince those Gods to get their priests to agitate against it, but more importantly, they could curse the city with disaster, and say they'll lift it when the slave trade is banned, and then if it's banned bless the city with various useful blessings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T12:11:09-08:00","id":1267045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266497-on-fighting-slavery-with-words-plot-help?p=1267025#post1267025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something else to consider for Exalted in terms of banning slavery.<br /> Looking at history again, and to quote a priest involved in the Abolition Society: <br /> <br /> Essentially, Gods are a powerful force, and may bless or curse people<br /> <br /> If the PCs can find some spirits who hate the slave trade for various reasons (it could be because they're God of Freedom or something, but it could also be random stuff, like, for example, slaves don't live in proper houses, so the God of Houses doesn't like the slave trade, or their use keeps costs in big plantations lower than those of smallholding farms, so the God of Freeholding Farms doesn't like them), they could convince those Gods to get their priests to agitate against it, but more importantly, they could curse the city with disaster, and say they'll lift it when the slave trade is banned, and then if it's banned bless the city with various useful blessings.</div> </div> </div> </div>This can go both ways though, the God of Slavery is <i>very nasty</i>. Likely on a shortlist of &quot;people in heaven you do NOT want to get on the bad side of.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T13:07:17-08:00","id":1267064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266497-on-fighting-slavery-with-words-plot-help?p=1266983#post1266983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If that was what you were saying, then, well, I disagree. Exalted's a roleplaying game, which means that considering the real participants' feelings and reactions is more important to me than an abstract consideration of &quot;what is absolutely the most realistic thing to happen&quot;. Slavery's a fraught subject, and deserves more careful handling than some others. Also, &quot;most realistic&quot; is, in my experience, something of an illusion in any case. &quot;Realism&quot; is quite often used to justify simply continuing our real-world prejudices in fiction (see umpteen-million arguments about how women can't be warriors, for instance, despite there being ample evidence that there <i>were</i> female warriors in the real world in basically all time periods). So I would avoid worrying too much about &quot;realistic&quot; consequences, and just remember that history contains plenty of times where things really did work out for the better, overall.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> One thing that speaks to how I see Exalted is that it is (generally, and with some exceptions) intended to be a hopeful game, especially in comparison to a great deal of White Wolf's other works, like Vampire (or God help us all, Wraith). Thus, unless your players agree to a different tone for the game, I think giving god-like beings god-like powers and a god-like mandate to go forth and change the world, and then screwing them when they do so for the sake of realism, is bad form at best. I feel like changing things should not always be easy or simple, but it should generally go well when the characters are doing what they're supposed to do, which is, in extremely broad and subjective terms, &quot;make the world a better place.&quot;<br /> <br /> Obviously, there are games where this is not appropriate - some Abyssal or Infernal games spring to mind - so YMMV.<br /> <br /> TL;DR - I side with Kelly in this debate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T14:49:58-08:00","id":1267093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1266497-on-fighting-slavery-with-words-plot-help?p=1267045#post1267045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This can go both ways though, the God of Slavery is <i>very nasty</i>. Likely on a shortlist of &quot;people in heaven you do NOT want to get on the bad side of.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly true! And if the PCs start a campaign to ban the slave trade, the merchants who are involved are likely to try and get their own divine support.<br /> <br /> Either way, definitely something for PCs to consider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpa